      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A novel series of fused-benzensulfonamide 2-N-(pyrazol-3-yl)methylbenzo[d]isothiazole-1,1-dioxide derivatives was designed and synthesized as metabolically stable T-type calcium channel inhibitors. Several compounds, 9, 10, and 17, displayed potent T-type channel inhibitory activity. Among them, compounds 10 and 17 showed good metabolic stability in human liver microsomes, and low hERG channel and CYP450 inhibition. Compound 10 exhibited diabetic neuropathic pain-alleviating effects in a streptozotocin-induced peripheral diabetic neuropathy (PDN) model. The maximum efficacy of compound 10, which was 3-fold more potent than gabapentin, was observed at 1h after administration, and co-administration of compound 10 with gabapentin showed a considerable synergic effect."
      },
